    "sha": "364e4b4f4005f79bf702c0cf1ffd82a6de4e57df",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVVonwNoAKDM2NGU0YjRmNDAwNWY3OWJmNzAyYzBjZjFmZmQ4MmE2ZGU0ZTU3ZGY",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-20T15:18:01Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-20T15:18:01Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(import): the STEP edge-gap cap follows the tolerance that the file states\n\nThe cap on how far an edge may lie off its face's surface is now twice\nthe distance uncertainty that the file states (converted to mm), from\n0.01 mm to a hard limit of 0.02 mm. A file that states no uncertainty\nkeeps 0.01 mm. The refusal names the gap, the cap and its source, and a\nkept gap over 0.01 mm is noted.\n\nA model whose edge gaps stop the mesh at the import chord is meshed once\nat twice the stated tolerance (at most 0.02 mm). The importer hands out\nthat chord, so the #864 reduced-fidelity flag marks the model, and a\nplain note names the gap and the file's tolerance.\n\nPinned by our own generated fixtures (testdata/models/edge_gap/) at the\nkernel, the importer and the app. Decision: docs/decisions/2976-edge-gap-cap.md.\n\nRefs #917\nFixes #2976\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
